# Citation File Format (CFF)
# Use this file to cite this software in academic publications
# More info: https://citation-file-format.github.io/

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'Biometric Authentication & Anti-Spoofing Security Research System'
message: 'If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below.'
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: 'Your Last Name'
    given-names: 'Your First Name'
    # email: your.email@example.com
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
    # affiliation: 'Your Institution'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/yourusername/biometric-security-research'
url: 'https://github.com/yourusername/biometric-security-research'
abstract: >-
  A comprehensive biometric security research platform that demonstrates
  both offensive (red team) and defensive (blue team) capabilities.
  This system implements face and fingerprint authentication, systematically
  tests against presentation attacks (photo, video, 3D mask, deepfakes,
  adversarial attacks), and evaluates anti-spoofing defenses with
  comprehensive security metrics.
keywords:
  - biometric authentication
  - face recognition
  - fingerprint matching
  - anti-spoofing
  - liveness detection
  - presentation attacks
  - adversarial attacks
  - security research
  - computer vision
  - machine learning
  - deepfake detection
license: MIT
version: '2.0.0'
date-released: '2024-11-14'

